{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.A3CrossTermMagnitudeClosed.geom_offblock_gives_magnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.A3CrossTermMagnitudeClosed.geom_offblock_gives_magnitude","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.lean#L192-L192","doc":"The geometrically-derived off-block `B_geom` (an input from the DM q-cubic,\nNOT tuned to the target) drives the even-face correction to the physical\ncross-sector magnitude `κ_phys`, which is a genuine lift (`≠ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.A3CrossTermMagnitudeClosed.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.A3CrossTermMagnitudeClosed.mk","kind":"ctor","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.lean#L187-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.A3CrossTermMagnitudeClosed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.A3CrossTermMagnitudeClosed","kind":"class","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.lean#L164-L193","doc":"**§3b dependent target conjecture — the A=3 magnitude closes via a DERIVED\noff-block.**\n\n`@conjecture: dependent` (its content depends on the open DM-cubic derivation of\nthe off-blocks — `conj:qdifference-kernel-prolongation-symbol` / the `qou-jqof`\nwall — supplying `B_geom`).\n\nThe claim: the off-block value `B_geom` **supplied by the geometry** (the DM\nq-cubic period datum, an INPUT independent of the physical target) yields exactly\nthe physical cross-sector magnitude `κ_phys` on the even face, and `κ_phys ≠ 1`\n(a genuine lift, matching `r* ≈ 1.585 ≠ 1`).\n\n**Why this is content-bearing and NOT the fit.**  In a *fit*, `B` is solved from\n`κ_phys` (`crossTerm_magnitude_surjective`).  Here `B_geom` is a *given*\n(geometric) input and the equation `evenFaceCorrection A (crossTerm B_geom C D) =\nκ_phys` is a nontrivial *check* that the geometry lands the physics — false for a\ngeneric `B_geom`.  **No instance is supplied**: the framework does not yet derive\n`B_geom` (that derivation IS the open keystone).  Discharging this by *choosing*\n`B_geom` to hit `κ_phys` would be the forbidden fit and is explicitly not done. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.crossTerm_magnitude_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.crossTerm_magnitude_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.lean#L134-L154","doc":"**THE DECISIVE INVARIANT — the cross-term magnitude is a FREE parameter\n(sorry-free).**  For fixed nonzero even/odd blocks `A, C, D`, the map\n`B ↦ evenFaceCorrection A (crossTerm B C D)` is **surjective** onto `R`: for\n*any* target value `r` there is an off-block `B` realizing it.  Concretely the\nwitness is `B = A·(1 − r)·D·C⁻¹`, which drives the cross-term to `A·(1 − r)` and\nthe correction to `r`.\n\n**Consequence (the honest verdict).**  The A=3 magnitude factor `r*` is not\n*derived* by the Berezinian cross-term — it is one real constraint on an\nunconstrained off-block, i.e. a **fit**.  Bar-oddness already forces the two\noff-blocks `B, C` to be independent (`BerezinianSelfAdjointCrossTerm`), so the\nroute carries ≥ 2 free amplitudes and can hit any sign *and* any magnitude.\nDeriving `B, C` from the DM q-cubic period datum (`qou-jqof`) is the open wall;\nabsent it, `r*` is a hidden DOF. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.evenFaceCorrection_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.evenFaceCorrection_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.lean#L122-L132","doc":"**A lift requires a nonzero cross-term (sorry-free).**  For `A ≠ 0`, the\neven-face correction equals `1` **iff** the cross-term vanishes.  So any\nmagnitude coefficient `≠ 1` (in particular `r* ≈ 1.585`) is possible ONLY through\na nonzero even↔odd mixing term — never from the diagonal (single-trace) data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.evenFaceCorrection_no_mixing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.evenFaceCorrection_no_mixing","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.lean#L112-L120","doc":"**No mixing ⇒ no lift (sorry-free).**  With the off-block `B = 0` the cross-term\nvanishes and the even-face correction is identically `1` (for `A ≠ 0`): a\nblock-diagonal / single-trace ingredient supplies **no** magnitude lift.  This\nis the structural reason every single-Markov-trace A=3 ingredient is bracketed\nat the same coefficient — none of them can move it.  The lift must come from the\ncross-term, which is off-diagonal by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.evenFaceCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.evenFaceCorrection","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.lean#L106-L110","doc":"The multiplicative **even-face correction** the cross-term supplies to the\nbar-even (mass / C1) face: `(A − t)/A` where `t` is the cross-term.  Equals `1`\nexactly when there is no mixing (`t = 0`); the A=3 magnitude claim is that this\ncorrection equals `r* ≈ 1.585`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.crossTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.crossTerm","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SuperBerezinianA3Magnitude.lean#L101-L104","doc":"The Berezinian **cross-term** `t = B·D⁻¹·C` — the first even↔odd mixing order\n(grade-reversing off-blocks `B, C` bridged by the odd block inverse `D⁻¹`).\nVanishes exactly at block-diagonal / single-trace order (`B = 0` or `C = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}